" [:option {:value "2"} "1900 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "3"} "1904 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "4"} "1906  Intercalated Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "5"} "1908 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "6"} "1912 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "7"} "1920 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "8"} "1924 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "9"} "1928 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "10"} "1932 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "11"} "1936 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "12"} "1948 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "13"} "1952 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "14"} "1956 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "15"} "1960 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "16"} "1964 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "17"} "1968 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "18"} "1972 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "19"} "1976 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "20"} "1980 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "21"} "1984 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "22"} "1988 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "23"} "1992 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "24"} "1996 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "25"} "2000 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "26"} "2004 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "53"} "2008 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "65"} "2010 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "67"} "2014 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "59"} "2016 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "69"} "2018 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "61"} "2020 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "63"} "2024 Summer Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/ROW'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Rowing at the 2012 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "28 July –  4 August 2012"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "14"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/860"} "Eton Dorney, Windsor"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "Rowing at the 2012 Summer Olympics took place at Dorney Lake, known as Eton Dorney during the Games, a private man-made lake owned by Eton College, where the Games’ sprint canoe events were also held. The majority of the spots, awarded to the NOCs rather than individual athletes, were based off of the results of the 2011 World Championships and the event lineup, eight for men and six for women, remained the same as it had been since 1996. Great Britain improved upon their success in Beijing, where it was the most successful nation in rowing, and was far and away the dominant force at its home Olympics, winning nine medals overall, four of which were gold. Three of those went to women’s teams, making it the first time the nation’s women had won Olympic rowing gold. British boats reached 13 of 14 finals with the sole exception being the women’s single sculls where there was no entry. New Zealand was a respectable runner-up in the medal count, with five total, three of which were gold. The Kiwi successes included the coxless pair of " [:a {:href "/athletes/104360"} "Eric Murray"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/112414"} "Hamish Bond"] " who were amongst the most dominant victors not just in this sport, but of the whole Games. " [:a {:href "/athletes/112434"} "Kim Crow"] " of Australia was a force in the women’s events as, with silver in the double scull and bronze in the single, she was the only rower at the regatta to win more than one medal. Another notable victory was that of South Africa’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/121634"} "Sizwe Ndlovu"] " who, as part of his nation’s lightweight coxless four, became the first black African Olympic rowing champion."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Crowds at the rowing venue were unusually large and noisy, which created an effect known as the “Dorney Roar” most noticeably when a home crew was in contention. This reached a crescendo during the final of the women’s double sculls where home favourite " [:a {:href "/athletes/92558"} "Katherine Grainger"] " won her first Olympic title after three successive silver medals."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/319061"} "Single Sculls, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "28 July –  3 August 2012"] "\n" [:td {} "33"] "\n" [:td {} "33"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/319027"} "Double Sculls, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "28 July –  2 August 2012"] "\n" [:td {} "26"] "\n" [:td {} "13"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/319094"} "Coxless Pairs, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "28 July –  3 August 2012"] "\n" [:td {} "26"] "\n" [:td {} "13"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/319107"} "Quadruple Sculls, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "28 July –  3 August 2012"] "\n" [:td {} "52"] "\n" [:td {} "13"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/319191"} "Coxless Fours, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "30 July –  4 August 2012"] "\n" [:td {} "52"] "\n" [:td {} "13"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/319000"} "Eights, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "28 July –  1 August 2012"] "\n" [:td {} "72"] "\n" [:td {} "8"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/319171"} "Lightweight Double Sculls, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "29 July –  4 August 2012"] "\n" [:td {} "40"] "\n" [:td {} "20"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/319040"} "Lightweight Coxless Fours, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {}